        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: A FULL BLEED HEALTH CHECK OF ENG #1 COMPONENTS WAS SCHEDULED DUE TO NO BLEED PX IN ALL STAGES OF FLIGHT. PRSOV WAS FOUND IN LOCKED CLOSED POSITION AND WAS ACTIVATED REF W/O 102146437

ACMS STILL SHOWS L/H BLEED ANOMALY DURING CLIMB ON ALL FLIGHTS. HEALTH CHECK TO BE PERFORMED.

ACTION:  
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
	
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
	
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
	
3. INSPECT ALL SYSTEM SENSE LINES AND CONNECTIONS FOR ANY SIGNS OF DAMAGE, BLOCKAGE OR LEAKAGE. MAKE THE NECESSARY RECTIFICATIONS.

4.CHECK  DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE PN 16135-81 FOR OBSTRUCTION USING COMPRESSED NITROGEN. 

5. LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:
	A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE
	B) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV
	C) SUPPLY SENSE LINE TO HSR
	D) SENSE LINE TO PRSOV
	E) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR 
	F) 390 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION

6. IF NFF, REPLACE ENG #1 BAR IAW 36-11-03/401 - LATEST REV

7. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.</description>
